msgid "Default versions of dependencies"
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-default-versions.rst:13
msgid ""
"Read the Docs supports any documentation tool to build your "
"documentation. However, we provide pre-defined builders for `Sphinx "
"<https://www.sphinx-doc.org/>`__ and `MkDocs "
"<https://www.mkdocs.org/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-default-versions.rst:17
msgid ""
"In the past we used to install several dependencies to a specific version"
" and update them after some time, but doing so would break some builds "
"and make it more difficult for new projects to use new versions. For this"
" reason, we are now installing just the minimal required dependencies "
"using their latest version by default. You can see the full list of "
"historical dependencies and advice for migrating in our `blog post "
"<https://blog.readthedocs.com/defaulting-latest-build-tools/>`__ "
"announcing this change."
msgstr ""

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/build-default-versions.rst:24
msgid ""
"In order to keep your builds reproducible, it's highly recommended "
"declaring its dependencies and versions explicitly. See :doc:`/guides"
"/reproducible-builds`."
msgstr ""

